set -eu
cd "${LAB_DIR:-.}"
cat > postmortem.md <<'EOT'
# Postmortem: checkout errors after deploy v212

## Summary
A config template typo set the database connection pool of checkout to 4 instead of 40. After deploy v212 the 5xx ratio reached 9 percent until a rollback restored service.

## Impact
About 16 minutes of elevated errors on checkout, peaking at 9 percent of requests.

## Timeline
- 02:05Z deploy of v212 finishes
- 02:10Z HighErrorRatio pages the primary on-call
- 02:14Z dashboard and journal show an exhausted connection pool
- 02:18Z evidence saved (journal export, thread dump), rollback to v211 started
- 02:21Z error ratio under 0.5 percent
- 02:40Z incident closed
minutes_to_mitigate=11

## Root cause
The configuration template allowed a pool size of 4 and nothing validated it. The deploy check sent one request, which a pool of 4 serves.

## Contributing factors
The runbook did not list rollback as the first mitigation. The alert fired five minutes after errors began because of its for clause.

## What went well
The page was acknowledged in one minute, evidence was saved before the rollback, and the rollback worked first time.

## What went badly
Recovery waited for a manual search for the rollback command. The deploy check could not detect a small pool.

## Action items
- Validate pool size bounds in the config template tests | owner: checkout-team | due: 2026-12-01 | class: prevent
- Add a load-shaped smoke test to the deploy pipeline | owner: platform | due: 2026-12-15 | class: detect
- Put the rollback command first in the HighErrorRatio runbook | owner: sre | due: 2026-11-30 | class: mitigate
EOT
